From 356e013b544ad7719c156730319d442585258047 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:14:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] library: a project whose folder was deleted outside magpie
 comes off the list when it's removed (#3510)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RemoveProject empties a project (Skills, Servers, then syncProject) and
takes the entry off the list only once nothing magpie placed or wrote is
left in it. But the only thing that empties those records, syncProject,
gives up on a folder that's gone: it says "the folder is gone" and
returns with the records as they were — and the Result RemoveProject
hands it is thrown away, so the removal itself says nothing; the toast
the user sees is the one the full sync after every change reports. With
the folder gone there is nothing magpie can ever take back, so the
records never empty and the entry stays for good: the only way out was
the keep checkbox, which takes the entry off the list without looking at
the folder (#514), though that reads as keeping what magpie wrote, not
as the way out of a dead removal.

So removal now does what a skill's removal already does when its folder
is gone (removeSkill: only the entry goes): a folder that isn't there
has nothing of magpie's on disk to take back, so the project and the
records of what it placed and wrote go together, and the removal says
nothing failed. A folder that is there removes as before; a project
gone from disk still shows its "folder is gone" badge and still reports
the folder on a full sync; keep is untouched.

TestRemoveProjectWhoseFolderIsGone is new: a project with placed skills
whose folder is deleted outside magpie, removed without keep — the
entry goes, the Result has no problem, the library's skills stay; and a
gone project removed with keep goes off the list as it always did. It
fails without the change (the removal says "the folder is gone" and the
entry stays) and passes with it.

go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/library/ pass (28 project and
gone-family tests targeted first); gofmt, go vet -tags nogui and
go build -tags nogui ./... pass. The cgo warning from
internal/gui/trayimage_darwin.go is there before this change.

